use the operator withholds it. The absence of a send also follows from the source: retainAndSendOriginal writes originals/initialize-policy.json before it sends, line 127 runs before that call, and no such file exists. The intent was signed with a 120 s lifetime, never left the process, and has expired.\n\nThe same line is in the v9 operator.mjs. No test or qualifier ran dispatch() through to its send, so no earlier review could see this. Check the V11 enrollment source for the same declaration; I did not find operator.mjs at the top of that source directory.\n\nRequested successor, with your numbering:\n1. Rename the inner variable in dispatch(), and change nothing else in the operator.\n2. Add a synthetic witness that runs dispatch() through retainAndSendOriginal against a fake transport. It must fail on the v10 bytes and pass on the successor.\n3. Use a new once namespace and label. Leave continuation-v10, its HALTED.json and its capture unchanged. Bind the successor to this halt receipt.\n4. Keep the policy candidate 23dad390 and approval 84be575c. The successor must still read published null before it acts.\n5. Release one argv at a time, as before. I run each one once.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}